          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider the expansion for",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p28-q1-expansion",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "(1+x)^4={}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1x+{}^{4}C_2x^2+{}^{4}C_3x^3+{}^{4}C_4x^4\\qquad(*)",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p28-q1-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Use it to prove the following results and interpret the result in terms of the row 1 4 6 4 1 on Pascal’s triangle.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By substituting $x=1$, show that ${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4=2^4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4=2^4=16$. The sum of all entries in the row is $16$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+1)^4&={}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4\\\\2^4&={}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4\\end{align*}$$\nThis is the sum of all entries in the row: $1+4+6+4+1=16$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By substituting $x=-1$, show that ${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4={}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4={}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_3=8$. Entries with even indices and entries with odd indices have equal sums.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1-1)^4&={}^{4}C_0-{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2-{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4\\\\0&={}^{4}C_0-{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2-{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4\\end{align*}$$\nRearranging gives\n$$ {}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4={}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_3. $$\nThe alternating sum is zero, so the sum of entries with even indices $(0,2,4)$ equals the sum of entries with odd indices $(1,3)$: $1+6+1=4+4=8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, by using the results of parts a and b, show that ${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4=2^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "${}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4=2^3=8$. The sum of entries with even indices is half the sum of the whole row.",
          "worked": "From part a:\n$$ {}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_3+{}^{4}C_4=2^4. $$\nFrom part b:\n$$ {}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4={}^{4}C_1+{}^{4}C_3. $$\nSubstituting the result of part b into part a:\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\left({}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4\\right)&=2^4\\\\{}^{4}C_0+{}^{4}C_2+{}^{4}C_4&=2^3\\end{align*}$$\nThe sum of entries with even indices $(0,2,4)$ is half the sum of the whole row: $1+6+1=8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      }
    ]
  },
